12:["$","section","What is the acceptable period for UK study gaps?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"What is the acceptable period for UK study gaps?"}],[["$","p","The UK is well known for always being a very supportive and welcoming country for international students who want to pursue their higher education. The UK accepts study gaps for a specific number of years. The UK accepts different time periods for study gaps when pursuing a bachelor’s degree and a postgraduate degree.",{"children":"The UK is well known for always being a very supportive and welcoming country for international students who want to pursue their higher education. The UK accepts study gaps for a specific number of years. The UK accepts different time periods for study gaps when pursuing a bachelor’s degree and a postgraduate degree."}],["$","p","Bachelor’s Degree: Students with a maximum study gap of 2 years can apply to any university in the UK. Certain universities allow students who have a 3-year study gap to pursue their education despite the 3-year study gap. If you have a fundamental cause for the year gap, many UK universities will accept your application.",{"children":"Bachelor’s Degree: Students with a maximum study gap of 2 years can apply to any university in the UK. Certain universities allow students who have a 3-year study gap to pursue their education despite the 3-year study gap. If you have a fundamental cause for the year gap, many UK universities will accept your application."}],["$","p","Postgraduate Degree: Students who have a five-year study gap after their bachelor’s degree can apply to universities in the UK. If your year gap does not exceed 5 years, the likelihood of rejection is relatively low. For postgraduate aspirants, if your study gap is more than 10–15 years, there is no need to worry; if you have all the valid reasons and documents of proof to justify your gap, the universities will still welcome you.",{"children":"Postgraduate Degree: Students who have a five-year study gap after their bachelor’s degree can apply to universities in the UK. If your year gap does not exceed 5 years, the likelihood of rejection is relatively low. For postgraduate aspirants, if your study gap is more than 10–15 years, there is no need to worry; if you have all the valid reasons and documents of proof to justify your gap, the universities will still welcome you."}],["$","p","Students can fill in the huge gap by pursuing a diploma or any pre-masters course, which can act as a bridge to study in the UK more easily.",{"children":"Students can fill in the huge gap by pursuing a diploma or any pre-masters course, which can act as a bridge to study in the UK more easily."}],["$","p","There are 4 different methods to bridge the study gap:",{"children":"There are 4 different methods to bridge the study gap:"}],["$","p","The students who have exceeded the study-year time period can bridge the year with different methods. Bridging the study gap can make your application process much easier. You should clearly explain the various methods to the immigration officer and the university to which you have applied to ensure a smoother process.",{"children":"The students who have exceeded the study-year time period can bridge the year with different methods. Bridging the study gap can make your application process much easier. You should clearly explain the various methods to the immigration officer and the university to which you have applied to ensure a smoother process."}],"$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35","$L36","$L37"],"$L38"]}]
